nd has very low equity against a random opponent hand. While heads-up play allows for a wider range of playable hands, 4-6 off-suit is typically at the bottom of the folding range. Calling (investing more chips) would rely heavily on outplaying the opponent post-flop with weak holdings, which is risky. Since there are still 9 hands remaining after this one, preserving chips for a higher equity spot is the best strategy to overcome the current deficit.\n\nReason: The hand is too weak to justify matching the big blind bet. Folding minimizes loss (50 chips) and preserves the stack for better opportunities in future hands.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
